  "description": "<strong>A. SUMMARY </strong>\nAll transit stops in the SFMTA system (e.g. Muni bus and transit stops).\n\n<strong>B. METHODOLOGY  </strong>\nStop data is exported from the Trapeze scheduling system and represents the most up to date location of transit stops. \n\n<strong>C. UPDATE FREQUENCY  </strong>\nUpdated by “Sign-up”, when transit system changes are put into effect. Updates range from every 3-6 months.\n\n<strong>D. HOW TO USE THIS DATASET </strong>\nThis dataset is derived from the GTFS data that the SFMTA makes available via <u><a href=\"https://511.org/open-data/transit\">Metropolitan Transit Commission's 511 Open Transit Data Portal</a></u>. GTFS files are the standard way to communicate transit schedules, and include the schedule for trips, stop locations, and route paths. The SFMTA publish"
